      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(msteams): cap team-group-id cache with pruneMapToMaxSize",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `teamGroupIdCache` Map in `resolveTeamGroupId` had TTL-based expiry (10 min) but no size cap. A large Teams workspace with many distinct team IDs could accumulate entries faster than the TTL window, allowing unbounded growth.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdded a 500-entry cap via `pruneMapToMaxSize` — the shared SDK helper already used by 11 other files. The cap is applied after each successful cache insert.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo change for normal usage. Memory usage bounded at ~500 entries regardless of workspace size.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Vitest regression — `resolveTeamGroupId` capped at 500 through mocked Graph responses\n\nThe test mocks `fetchGraphJson` to return successful Graph responses, calls `resolveTeamGroupId` 501 times with distinct team IDs, and verifies the cache cap works:\n\n```text\n$ pnpm vitest run --project extension-msteams extensions/msteams/src/graph-thread.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n\n ✓ resolveTeamGroupId > caps cache at 500 entries — evicts oldest on overflow\n ... 21 passed (21)\n```\n\nThe test exercises the full `resolveTeamGroupId` path:\n- Fills 500 entries through successful mocked Graph lookups\n- 501st entry triggers `pruneMapToMaxSize` → oldest entry (team-0) evicted\n- Verifies team-0 is re-fetched from Graph (eviction proof)\n- Verifies team-1 is still cached (LRU semantics)\n\n### Lint\n\n```text\n$ npx oxlint extensions/msteams/src/graph-thread.ts\n0 errors, 0 warnings\n```\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex",
